{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 10: a truck fleet as a three-stage ageing chain (new, mid-life, old). Retired trucks are replaced. The fleet was bought all at once, so retirements and maintenance costs come in echoes. }
Stage Time=
	4
	~	year
	~	Average years a truck spends in each age class.
	|
New Trucks= INTEG(
	Purchases - Ageing to Mid,
	300)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks up to about 4 years old.
	|
Ageing to Mid=
	New Trucks / Stage Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Mid Trucks= INTEG(
	Ageing to Mid - Ageing to Old,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 4 to 8 years.
	|
Ageing to Old=
	Mid Trucks / Stage Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Old Trucks= INTEG(
	Ageing to Old - Retirements,
	0)
	~	truck
	~	Trucks of about 8 years and over.
	|
Retirements=
	Old Trucks / Stage Time
	~	truck/year
	~	|
Purchases=
	Retirements
	~	truck/year
	~	Every retired truck is replaced at once.
	|
Fleet=
	New Trucks + Mid Trucks + Old Trucks
	~	truck
	~	|
Cost New=
	2
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	Maintenance cost of a new truck.
	|
Cost Mid=
	6
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Cost Old=
	14
	~	kUSD/truck/year
	~	|
Maintenance Cost=
	Cost New * New Trucks + Cost Mid * Mid Trucks + Cost Old * Old Trucks
	~	kUSD/year
	~	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ year ~ |
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ year ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ year ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ year ~ |
